add('company/who','Who we are',`<p style="font:italic 22px Georgia,serif;color:var(--green)">Grow Value. Feed Purpose. Cultivate Impact.</p><p>BeraDeb Nexus Limited is a Nigerian agribusiness company (RC 8425979). Our office is in Lagos and our farms are in Odeda Local Government Area, Ogun State.</p><p>We connect land, capital, farming expertise and markets. Our work covers crop production and farm management, the Farm Syndicate, produce supply and distribution, agro-processing as we grow, and technology and digital-skills education for young people.</p><h2>Our Vision</h2><p>To become a leading and transformative enterprise advancing agricultural productivity, food security, economic prosperity, and sustainable development through innovation, strategic partnerships, and purposeful investments.</p><h2>Our Mission</h2><p>To unlock agricultural potential by connecting land, capital, knowledge, technology, and strategic partnerships to build productive agricultural assets, strengthen food value chains, create sustainable economic opportunities, and empower individuals and communities through agriculture and education.</p><h2>Our Core Values</h2><ul style="list-style:none;padding:0"><li><b>1. Integrity</b><br>We uphold honesty, transparency, and ethical conduct in all our dealings, building lasting relationships founded on trust, credibility, and mutual respect.</li><li><b>2. Excellence</b><br>We pursue quality, professionalism, and continuous improvement, striving to deliver exceptional value across our operations and engagements.</li><li><b>3. Innovation</b><br>We embrace creativity, technology, and progressive thinking to develop practical solutions that enhance agricultural productivity and address evolving business and societal needs.</li><li><b>4. Collaboration</b><br>We believe meaningful and sustainable progress is achieved through strategic partnerships, shared knowledge, mutual respect, and collective commitment.</li><li><b>5. Accountability</b><br>We take ownership of our decisions, responsibilities, and outcomes, promoting responsible resource management, transparency, and commitment to our obligations.</li><li><b>6. Sustainability</b><br>We promote responsible agricultural practices and sustainable business models that preserve resources, strengthen food systems, and create lasting value for present and future generations.</li><li><b>7. Impact</b><br>We are purpose-driven in our pursuit of growth, committed to contributing to food security, economic empowerment, youth development, and inclusive prosperity.</li></ul><h2>Our Corporate Philosophy</h2><p>At BeraDeb Nexus Limited, we believe that sustainable prosperity begins with recognising potential and creating the structures, partnerships, and opportunities necessary to transform it into meaningful value.</p><p>We believe land can become productive assets, capital can unlock opportunities, knowledge can empower people, and technology can accelerate progress.</p><p>Our approach is rooted in purposeful enterprise, responsible partnerships, sustainable value creation, and the conviction that business growth should extend beyond financial returns to create meaningful economic and societal impact.</p><p>We are committed to building an enterprise where growth serves a purpose, partnerships create shared opportunities, and every endeavour contributes to a more productive, prosperous, and sustainable future.</p><h2>Our Brand Promise</h2><p><b>Grow Value. Feed Purpose. Cultivate Impact.</b></p><p>We create value through purposeful enterprise, advance meaningful opportunities through agriculture and education, and cultivate lasting impact through innovation, collaboration, and sustainability.</p>`);
add('company/leadership','Our Leadership and Team',`<div class="people"><div class="person"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Emmanuel Pentho Idowu"><h3>Emmanuel Pentho Idowu</h3><em>Co-Founder and CEO</em><p><b>Educationist | Entrepreneur | Leadership &amp; Development Professional | Counselling Psychology Practitioner</b></p><p>Emmanuel Pentho Idowu is a multidisciplinary professional, entrepreneur, educationist and development advocate with over a decade of professional experience spanning education, business development, operations management, technology-enabled learning, people development and organisational leadership.</p><p>He is the Co-Founder and Chief Executive Officer of BeraDeb Nexus Limited, an enterprise focused on agriculture, agribusiness development, investment partnerships and technology-driven empowerment. Through his leadership, he provides strategic direction, oversees business development and partnerships, and coordinates initiatives that connect agricultural opportunities with investment, innovation and sustainable value creation.</p><p>His professional experience cuts across the education, technology and business sectors. He previously served as a Schools Supervisor with NewGlobe (EkoExcel), where he supervised school operations, supported educational performance improvement, and trained over 15 Head Teachers and 300 teachers. He also served as Training and Innovation Manager at ZKTeco West Africa, coordinating digital learning programmes, managing learning management systems and supporting training and certification initiatives. His experience further includes human resource management, recruitment, stakeholder engagement and organisational development.</p><p>Beyond corporate and entrepreneurial leadership, Emmanuel is passionate about human development, relationships, emotional wellbeing and purposeful living. He is the Founder of The Seed Community, a relationship and personal development community committed to helping individuals build healthier relationships, develop meaningful connections and approach life with greater understanding, responsibility and purpose. His interests in counselling psychology, family development, career growth and leadership inform his commitment to creating platforms that support personal and interpersonal transformation.</p><p>Academically, he holds a Bachelor of Science in Education (Political Science Education) from Lagos State University and has postgraduate academic training in Counselling Psychology. He is also a Fellow of the Teachers Registration Council of Nigeria (TRCN) and has professional development experience in AWS cloud technology, technological development and digital learning.</p><p>Emmanuel is also a writer and author of <i>Developing Intimacy with the Holy Spirit</i> and <i>Unscripted Relationship</i>. His interest in combining technology with human development is further reflected in MindNexus, a web-based counselling platform initiative.</p><p>At the heart of his work is a commitment to developing people, strengthening institutions, building sustainable enterprises and creating opportunities for individuals and communities to grow. He believes that meaningful development happens when knowledge, leadership, innovation and purpose work together to produce lasting impact.</p></div><div class="person"><img src="data:image/jpeg;base64," alt="Oluwayanmife Deborah Idowu"><h3>Oluwayanmife Deborah Idowu</h3><em>Co-Founder and General Manager / COO</em><p><b>Operations, Supply Chain and Quality Management Professional.</b></p><p>A versatile, results-driven professional with a background in Biochemistry, Supply Chain Management, Brewing Operations, Quality Assurance and Business Administration. She has worked across the FMCG, food and beverage, and manufacturing sectors, with hands-on experience in production operations, logistics, inventory management, procurement, quality control and process improvement. She has supervised operational teams and promoted